<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <.header>
    How {@organisation.name} uses your data in Rescord
    <:subtitle>The privacy notice of {@organisation.name}</:subtitle>
  </.header>

  <p :if={@missing != []} id="notice-missing" role="status">
    {@organisation.name} has not finished this notice yet. Ask them about your data in the
    meantime.
  </p>

  <article :if={@missing == []} id="notice">
    <p>
      {@organisation.name} uses Rescord to keep the records of its animals and the work of its
      volunteers. Rescord is run for us by {@server.operator_name}, on servers in {@server.hosting}.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="what-heading">
      <h2 id="what-heading">What we keep about you</h2>
      <p>
        Your email address, which you sign in with. The records you write and the changes you
        make, with your name on them, so that we know who cared for each animal. Expenses you
        record or are paid back for. Comments, and your conversations with the assistant if we
        use it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="why-heading">
      <h2 id="why-heading">Why</h2>
      <p>To run {@organisation.name} and care for its animals, and to keep our accounts.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="who-heading">
      <h2 id="who-heading">Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        The other members of {@organisation.name}. A partner refuge that receives an animal
        gets a copy of its records, without your name. Emails go through {@server.mail_provider}.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="long-heading">
      <h2 id="long-heading">How long</h2>
      <p>
        While you are a member. When you leave, your records stay with your name, marked as a
        former member<span :if={@settings.pseudonymise_after_months}>, and after {@settings.pseudonymise_after_months} months we replace your name with "Former member" and a number</span>.
        Expenses stay with your name for {@settings.money_years} years after each expense,
        because the law requires it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
      <h2 id="rights-heading">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see your data, to correct it, or to erase it. When we erase it, we remove
        your email address and your account, and replace your name on our records with
        "Former member" and a number. We keep what the law requires, such as money records, and
        tell you what and until when. Records you wrote about the animals stay, because the care
        of each animal depends on them. You can ask us to delete your comments.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our backups hold your data for {@server.backup_days} more days, and we never use them for
        anything else. If we ever restore a backup, Rescord erases you again before anybody uses
        it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ask-heading">
      <h2 id="ask-heading">How to ask</h2>
      <p>
        From the page Privacy of {@organisation.name} in Rescord, or by writing to
        <span :if={@settings.contact_name}>{@settings.contact_name}, at </span><a href={"mailto:#{@settings.contact_email}"}>{@settings.contact_email}</a>.
        We answer within one month.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="complaints-heading">
      <h2 id="complaints-heading">Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Write to us first.<span :if={@settings.authority}> You can also complain to {@settings.authority}.</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section :if={paragraphs(@settings.notice_text) != []} aria-labelledby="more-heading">
      <h2 id="more-heading">More from {@organisation.name}</h2>
      <p :for={paragraph <- paragraphs(@settings.notice_text)}>{paragraph}</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
